* {{audio|de|De-mein.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|aɪ̯n|s=1}}
* {{homophone|de|meinen}} {{a|according to a common pronunciation of this form}}

===Determiner===
{{head|de|determiner|cat2=possessive determiners}}

# {{lb|de|possessive}} [[my]]

====Declension====
{{de-decl-pronoun<!--
-->|mein|meine|mein|meine<!--
-->|meines|meiner|meines|meiner<!--
-->|meinem|meiner|meinem|meinen<!--
-->|meinen|meine|mein|meine<!--
-->}}

When used as a possessive pronoun, the nominative masculine takes the form {{m|de|meiner}}, which equals English "mine", and the nominative/accusative neuter takes the form {{m|de|meines}} or {{m|de|meins}}.
* dein Vater und '''meiner''' – your father and mine
* dein Kind und '''mein'''(e)'''s''' – your child and mine
When the pronoun is placed after a noun, it is left uninflected:
* Gen Himmel zu dem Vater '''mein''' fahr ich von diesem Leben (song ''Nun freut euch, lieben Christen g'mein'') – Towards Heaven to my father go I from this life.

